File: assets/css/formComponents.css

=======================================================================
Section 1 — .vCheckboxWrapper
OLD_SECTION
.vCheckboxWrapper {
    height:auto;
    display:block;

NEW_SECTION
.vCheckboxWrapper {
    /* height:auto; */ /* would override the generated .v<className> height (the link loads after the generated styles) and collapse the widget — same fix as .vRadioButtonWrapper above */
    display:block;

REASON
The static sheet always loads after the generated per-class styles, so height:auto beat
the generated .v<className>{height:...} and every checkbox widget collapsed to
<width>x0 — invisible and unclickable. The radio wrapper had the identical line already
commented out; this applies the same fix to the checkbox.

=======================================================================
Section 2 — .vRadioButtonWrapper .vRadioButton::before
OLD_SECTION
.vRadioButtonWrapper .vRadioButton::before {
position:absolute;
border-radius:100%;

NEW_SECTION
.vRadioButtonWrapper .vRadioButton::before {
content:''; /* without this the pseudo-element never renders and radios are invisible — the checkbox rule below already had it */
position:absolute;
border-radius:100%;

REASON
The pseudo-element that draws the radio circle had no content property, so it never
generated and radios were invisible out of the box (labels only). The equivalent
checkbox rule already had content:''.

=======================================================================
Section 3 — date picker control buttons (after the .rinactive rules)
OLD_SECTION
  .vDateBoxTool .vDateBoxControlCon .rinactive{
    cursor:not-allowed;
  }

NEW_SECTION
  .vDateBoxTool .vDateBoxControlCon .rinactive{
    cursor:not-allowed;
  }
  /* shared inactive class managed by ListScroller (it toggles one class on both buttons) */
  .vDateBoxTool .vDateBoxControlCon .vPrev.sInactive::before{
    border-right:15px solid #ccc;
  }
  .vDateBoxTool .vDateBoxControlCon .vNext.sInactive::before{
    border-left:15px solid #ccc;
  }
  .vDateBoxTool .vDateBoxControlCon .sInactive{
    cursor:not-allowed;
  }

REASON
ListScroller toggles ONE configured inactive class on both scroll buttons, but the CSS
only had per-side classes (linactive/rinactive) that nothing ever toggled. These rules
give the shared sInactive class (now configured by the date picker) the same greyed
appearance per side. The legacy linactive/rinactive rules are kept for compatibility.
